WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.459 --> 00:00:02.260
Welcome to Professor Dave Explains.

00:00:02.260 --> 00:00:04.830
I’m Dave, and this channel is for learning.

00:00:04.830 --> 00:00:07.259
There are a lot of YouTube channels for learning,
but this one is different.

00:00:07.259 --> 00:00:11.809
I’m not going to dazzle you with science-flavored
edutainment that’s fun to watch but falls

00:00:11.809 --> 00:00:13.510
short at delivering real knowledge.

00:00:13.510 --> 00:00:17.580
I’m also not going to just stand here and
lecture at a blackboard for two hours at a time.

00:00:17.620 --> 00:00:19.539
I want to give you something in between.

00:00:19.539 --> 00:00:25.149
The shortest, easiest route there has ever
been to a working understanding of everything

00:00:25.149 --> 00:00:30.329
around you, from the infinitesimally small
to the incomprehensibly large.

00:00:30.329 --> 00:00:34.340
I want to teach you chemistry, so you can
understand atoms and molecules.

00:00:34.340 --> 00:00:39.620
I want to teach you biochemistry, so you can
understand big molecules, like proteins and DNA.

00:00:39.720 --> 00:00:45.079
I want to teach you biology, so you can understand
the components that make up living organisms.

00:00:45.080 --> 00:00:51.180
I want to teach you physics, so you can understand the way the universe works on the most fundamental level.

00:00:51.240 --> 00:00:55.260
I want to teach you astronomy, so you can
understand all the fascinating objects we

00:00:55.269 --> 00:00:57.390
can see in this great big universe.

00:00:57.390 --> 00:01:01.600
I want to teach you mathematics, so you can
understand the important calculations that

00:01:01.600 --> 00:01:04.970
scientists have to perform, and reproduce them yourself.

00:01:04.970 --> 00:01:08.600
And that’s just the tip of the iceberg.

00:01:08.600 --> 00:01:10.570
But why bother learning all this stuff?

00:01:10.570 --> 00:01:14.549
Well for one thing, when you read about science-related
news, regarding nutrition, or medicine, or

00:01:14.549 --> 00:01:16.909
technology, wouldn’t you like to know what’s
going on?

00:01:16.909 --> 00:01:20.960
To make informed decisions for yourself, rather
than just repeating what others are saying?

00:01:20.960 --> 00:01:25.290
The only way to get there is to learn the
fundamentals, and this channel is the fastest

00:01:25.290 --> 00:01:26.310
way to do it.

00:01:26.310 --> 00:01:30.840
I cover typical high school and undergraduate
curricula, so if you’re a student, stick around.

00:01:30.840 --> 00:01:35.240
I will explain exactly what you are learning
in class in ways that will finally make sense.

00:01:35.240 --> 00:01:40.500
My tutorials are succinct, with animations
geared towards maximizing comprehension rather

00:01:40.500 --> 00:01:44.960
than amusement, and they stress the most important
details, while skipping all the fluff.

00:01:44.960 --> 00:01:49.710
It’s like I took your textbook and I’m
giving you the cliffs notes version, in easy-to-watch

00:01:49.710 --> 00:01:50.710
segments.

00:01:50.710 --> 00:01:55.060
And the best news is that because I focus
on the main concepts, my content is also great

00:01:55.060 --> 00:01:59.259
for anyone who just wants to learn science
without having to go to school or read a lot

00:01:59.259 --> 00:02:02.020
of books, and no prior knowledge is assumed.

00:02:02.020 --> 00:02:06.130
I’ll start you at the very beginning with
general chemistry, and you can climb the ladder

00:02:06.130 --> 00:02:07.200
from there.

00:02:07.200 --> 00:02:11.520
You may not find any explosions or songs or
flashy gimmicks along the way, but we don’t

00:02:11.520 --> 00:02:16.120
have time for that, we are here to understand
the universe, which is pretty fun in its own right.

00:02:16.180 --> 00:02:18.660
And it doesn’t matter who you are, either.

00:02:18.660 --> 00:02:23.100
Education is for everyone, and you should
want it, because knowledge is cool.

00:02:23.100 --> 00:02:27.040
With knowledge comes wisdom, and if everyone
can get wise enough, we can mold the world

00:02:27.040 --> 00:02:28.550
as we see fit.

00:02:28.550 --> 00:02:32.790
So subscribe to my channel for updates about
new content, support me on Patreon so I can

00:02:32.790 --> 00:02:36.060
make lots of it as fast as possible, and let’s
learn some science.

